It becomes obvious once you have kids how so many parents can unfortunately end up "neglecting" their kids; 

the most important thing that you can do for them is to be present, physically, emotionally, mentally; and we live in a world where as they get older, the poor only get more and more overwhelmed by life, and it's tremendously difficult to just revert that trend once you are no longer living on your own timing, let alone having the time to invest in yourself and taking risks;

and on the other side of the spectrum, the rich don't necessarily become better parents, because we don't live in such a fairy tale of a society that you can afford to relax and still remain competitive in whatever you strive to be the best at; and as a result, they outsource as much as they can, and end up spending way less time with their kids than they could have, and in retrospect, should have.
